course: dictionary
lesson: 6820
title: A word from nature
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name things you may never have seen. You can still work out what they mean by reading the words around them. «An osprey dives feet first into a lake to catch a fish.» Dives tells you it goes down fast, feet first tells you how, and lake and fish tell you where and why. So an osprey is a bird that catches fish.
explain: Clues also tell you what something looks like. «The osprey has brown wings and a white underside.» These words help you picture the bird. Check your guess by swapping your meaning into the sentence: a bird that catches fish fits, so you are on the right track.
explain: Context can tell you where something lives. «Ospreys live near lakes, rivers and coasts.» Water is the clue: they live where there is water and fish to eat. When you read about nature, ask what the animal does, what it looks like and where it lives.
fact: An osprey is a large bird of prey, which means it hunts other animals for food.
fact: Ospreys have brown wings and a white underside.
fact: An osprey dives feet first into water to catch fish.
fact: Ospreys live near lakes, rivers and coasts on every continent except Antarctica.
fact: Ospreys nearly died out in Britain, but they have come back, and people can watch their nests on webcams.
exercise: «An osprey dives feet first into a lake.» What does dives mean? | Flies high into the clouds | *Goes down quickly into the water | Sits still on a branch
exercise: Ospreys dive into water to catch fish. What do ospreys catch? | Insects | Frogs | *Fish
exercise: «The osprey has brown wings and a white underside.» Find and copy one word that tells you a colour. | osprey | *brown | underside | wings
test: Where do ospreys live? | In deserts, far from any water | Only high in the mountains | *Near lakes, rivers and coasts
test: «Ospreys nearly died out in Britain, but they have come back.» What does died out mean? | Grew very big | Flew away for a holiday | *Nearly all disappeared | Went for a long swim
exam: Which sentence best shows that an osprey is good at catching fish? | It lives on every continent except Antarctica | It was once rare in Britain | It has brown wings | *It dives feet first into a lake
